{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/676986-how-to-put-down-shartas","id":676986,"title":"How to put down Shartas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-24T16:18:30-07:00","id":676986,"title":"How to put down Shartas","content":"Since the Hosts have the annoying habit of turning themselves into bunches of vermin (rats, spiders, etc...) who slip away in every direction, and you have to make sure every single critter is eliminated so the Shartha doesn\u00b4t return...what tricks have the Urathas developed for the occasion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 09-25-2015, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T16:38:08-07:00","id":677017,"title":"","content":"Black Wolf, totem spirit of the Hunters in Darkness, is expressly called out to have designed traps for killing shartha, who even Father Wolf had trouble with.<br /> <br /> 'She taught her Father not to kill but to harry, to drive the swarms into dead ends and empty places where fire and falling rock could do the work of killing them.'<br /> <br /> If you look at the Hunter in Darkness gifts, mainly Nature and Warding, you can see really easy ways to corral the vermin into specific areas where you can then wipe them out. Elemental gifts probably come in handy for the more higher renowned Uratha. In my first game I set fire to a building with loads of rat shartha in it, which was a horrible idea as it was not an abandoned building at all. And later with another infestation the pack poured vast amounts of poison into another shartha nest, while in the Hisil spurred spirits of death and poison to further action.<br /> <br /> My character right now would probably have a very, very hard time to dealing with a swarm. His best chance for shartha would be while they were riding around in a human's body, where he'd just eat them. For a swarm I suppose he'd fall back on electrocution, wetting an area and waiting until they were in it to zap them. I don't think the eat-for-aggravated damage thing works for the 'final form' shartha.<br /> <br /> During the fiction in the book, which is a good depiction of the horror of the shartha, they <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">make a deal with a spirit to drown them all.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2015, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T17:00:56-07:00","id":677030,"title":"","content":"*Shartha (let me know if you'd like me to change that in the thread title)<br /> <br /> It sounds like the key is to be in tune with your territory, so you know right away when an infestation starts and everywhere individual shards might hide, and then to use the environment against them. Lay traps and focus the hunt on herding the Host(s) into them before delivering the final blow. Sure, they can Discorporate and scatter into a thousand shards, but what good does it do them if they have nowhere to scatter to?<br /> <br /> In general, anything with an area of effect is good against them. There are also a number of Gifts and other such abilities that are specifically helpful against Shartha. Knotted Paths is great for making sure no matter how many directions the shards run off in, they all eventually lead back to the place where you are waiting to ambush them. Read the World's Loom and Lore of the Land are both excellent for scanning a territory for Hosts that might otherwise slip past your radar. Of course, Boundary Ward is a great preventative measure (which as they say is worth a pound of cure.) The Nowhere to Run Merit can find where the vermin are nesting. And, of course, no Minanna pack should be without at least one Wolf-Blooded who has the Host Ache Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-24-2015, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T17:06:36-07:00","id":677033,"title":"","content":"Explosives, Flamethrowers, Movie-Constantine shenanigans, having friends with Swarm Form, Rain of Fire, Dragonfire, or any of the Graveyard (?) manifestations. Death, Forces, Matter, or any of the Elemental Contracts can also do the job, as would the Electrification and Vitality Transmutations. But in a focused Chronicle, dipping into the Gift of the Elementals, for fire, earth, or water, seems to be the kill shot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}